menu "BLE link"

    config BLE_LINK_NAME_PREFIX
        string "Advertising name prefix"
        default "IR-RMT"
        help
            The last two bytes of the Bluetooth MAC are appended, giving a name
            like "IR-RMT-1A2B" so several boards can be told apart. The name is
            advertised in the scan response, because a 128-bit service UUID
            already consumes most of the advertising payload.

    config BLE_LINK_RX_MAX
        int "Maximum inbound message size (bytes)"
        range 256 4096
        default 2048
        help
            Upper bound for a reassembled request. Larger requests are rejected.
            Two pool buffers plus one reassembly buffer of this size are reserved
            in static RAM.

    config BLE_LINK_TASK_PRIORITY
        int "Link task priority"
        range 1 20
        default 9

    config BLE_LINK_TASK_STACK
        int "Link task stack size (bytes)"
        range 2048 8192
        default 4096
        help
            The RX handler runs on this task, so the stack must cover JSON
            parsing and storage calls.

endmenu
